# Botan Workflow

## Configure and Build

Configure command (see `build/build_config.json` for the current one):

```
python3 configure.py --compiler-cache=ccache --build-tool=ninja --without-documentation --build-targets=static,tests,bogo_shim
```

- In-source-ish ninja build: `build.ninja` at repo root, objects in `build/obj/`, artifacts at root (`libbotan-3.a`, `botan-test`, `botan_bogo_shim`).
- Build tests + lib: `ninja tests -j9`. Library only: `ninja libbotan-3.a -j9`.
- **New source/test files require re-running `configure.py`** — sources are globbed at configure time and won't be picked up otherwise.
- Compile with zero warnings before considering a change done.
- For debug mode, add `--debug-mode`

## Running Tests

- `./botan-test --list-tests` lists all test suites.
- Run suites by name: `./botan-test dtls_record_layer_13_protected dtls_timers`.
- Full run: `./botan-test` (no args). Useful flags: `--test-threads=N`, `--skip-tests=a,b`, `--abort-on-first-fail`, `--run-long-tests`.
- If the full test binary ever fails to link and you need a quick partial one for a subset of test objects:
  `ls build/obj/test/*.o | tr '\n' ' ' > /tmp/tests_partial.txt && g++ -fstack-protector -m64 -pthread @/tmp/tests_partial.txt -L. -g -lbotan-3 -ldl -lrt -o /tmp/botan-test-partial`
  then run with `LD_LIBRARY_PATH=. /tmp/botan-test-partial <suite>`.

## Writing Tests

Read `src/tests/tests.h` before writing tests — it provides a lot of insfrastructure. Prefer the typed `Test::Result` predicates, which print produced-vs-expected values on failure:

- Typed equality/comparison: `test_sz_eq/lt/gte`, `test_u8/u16/u32/u64_eq`, `test_bin_eq` (also against a hex string), `test_bin_ne`, `test_str_eq/ne/contains`, `test_enum_eq`, `test_opt_*_eq`, `test_bn_eq` (BigInt), `test_rc` (FFI return codes).
- Exceptions: `result.test_throws<Botan::Invalid_Argument>("what", "expected message", [&] { ... })`, `test_no_throw`.
- Preconditions: `result.require("why", cond)` — aborts just this test (`Test_Aborted`) instead of crashing.
- Notes: `test_note(...)`, `note_missing(...)`.
- Small unit tests: wrap each case in an exception-safe scope and return them as a vector:
  `CHECK("descriptive name", [](Test::Result& result) { ... })` — an unexpected exception becomes a clean failure, not an abort.
- Register with `BOTAN_REGISTER_TEST(category, name, Test_Class)` or `BOTAN_REGISTER_TEST_FN(category, name, fn)`.
- Helpers: `Test::rng()`, `Test::data_dir(subdir)`, `Test::read_data_file(path)`; deterministic RNGs (`Fixed_Output_RNG`, `Fixed_Output_Position_RNG`) live in `src/tests/test_rng.h`.
- Data-driven KAT tests: derive from `Text_Based_Test` and put vectors in `src/tests/data/`. Prefer test vectors generated by a third-party implementation over ones generated by Botan itself.

## BoGo (BoringSSL protocol test suite)

- Build target `bogo_shim` produces `./botan_bogo_shim` (source: `src/bogo_shim/bogo_shim.cpp`).
- Shim configs in `src/bogo_shim/config*.json` map expected BoGo failures/differences to reasons; update them when intentionally changing TLS behavior.
- Local runner (requires `go`): `python3 src/editors/vscode/scripts/bogo.py`
  - On first run clones Botan's BoringSSL fork into `build_deps/boringssl` (branch pinned in `src/scripts/repo_config.py`), then runs the BoGo runner.
  - Filter to specific tests by passing names through: `python3 src/editors/vscode/scripts/bogo.py -- 'Some-Test-Name'` (becomes `-debug -test '...'`).
  - Options: `--without-tls-12`, `--without-tls-13`, `--wait-for-debugger`.
- Manual equivalent: `cd build_deps/boringssl/ssl/test/runner && go test -pipe -allow-unimplemented -num-workers 16 -shim-path /workspaces/botan/botan_bogo_shim -shim-config /workspaces/botan/src/bogo_shim/config.json`.

## Formatting

- Use `clang-format-17` specifically.
- Format files you touched individually: `clang-format-17 -i <file>`. Do this BEFORE compiling; it is idempotent.
- The repo-wide script (`src/scripts/dev_tools/run_clang_format.py --clang-format-binary=clang-format-17 --src-dir=src/`) reformats unrelated pre-existing files — avoid unless doing a tree-wide cleanup.

## Coding Conventions

Distilled from `doc/dev_ref/contributing.rst` (read it for details):

- New files get a copyright header: `(C) 202x <You>` + "Botan is released under the Simplified BSD License (see license.txt)".
- Members are prefixed `m_`; declare variables `const` unless they change; use `override`/`final`; RAII instead of `new`/`delete`.
- Integers: `size_t` for values of no particular size; fixed-width `(u)intXX_t` only where the protocol/algorithm dictates the size.
- Braces on both sides of if/else; no `using namespace`; call OS/external functions via `::` (e.g. `::select`); `auto` only when the type is truly obvious.
- Comments: prefer restructuring code over long explanations; if behavior is dictated by an external standard, quote the RFC/NIST text verbatim with document and section. Doxygen doc-comments use `/** ... */`.
- Avoid complicated template metaprogramming; avoid external dependencies.
- clang-format config lives in `src/configs/clang-format`; exactly clang-format 17 is required; `// clang-format off` is allowed for truly horrible output.
- Git: don't merge master into topic branches — rebase and squash; small changes should be a single commit; non-trivial changes update `news.rst`.
- To keep blame clean: `git config --local blame.ignoreRevsFile src/configs/git-blame-ignore-revs`.

## Prefer Botan Helper Methods

Use the internal helpers instead of hand-rolling byte manipulation:

- `Botan::concat<OutR>(ranges...)` — concatenate byte ranges, e.g. `Botan::concat<std::vector<uint8_t>>(a, b)` (`botan/internal/concat_util.h`)
- `BufferSlicer` — parsing view over a byte buffer (`botan/internal/buffer_slicer.h`)
- `BufferStuffer` — append-only serialization into a fixed buffer (`botan/internal/buffer_stuffer.h`)
- `Botan::to_underlying(enum)` — enum to underlying integer (`botan/internal/stl_util.h`)
- `Botan::hex_decode` / `hex_encode` for test vectors (`botan/hex.h`)
- `Botan::CT` for constant-time programming
